---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';

const sections = [
  {
    heading: 'Tabletop background and editorial team',
    paragraphs: [
      'DnD Arena was founded and is curated by Alden Vance, a veteran Dungeon Master and narrative tabletop designer with more than twelve years of active campaign experience across fifth edition, classic d20 rulesets, and collaborative worldbuilding projects. Alden collaborates with contributing writers and campaign cartographers to design authentic, linguistically grounded sound palettes that reflect living fantasy worlds rather than random character strings.',
      'Our team tests every syllable matrix across active game sessions to verify that candidate names articulate cleanly during combat initiatives and feel natural across narrative roleplay scenes. We believe every adventurer, settlement, and guild deserves a moniker with real phonetic weight and immediate story potential.'
    ]
  },
  {
    heading: 'Built for the moment before a session',
    paragraphs: [
      'DnD Arena is an independent, browser-based fantasy naming workshop developed by veteran tabletop writers and Dungeon Masters to solve prep fatigue across tabletop roleplaying campaigns. Every generator in our catalog operates on handcrafted phonetic syllable tables tailored to distinct cultural, planar, and ancestral naming conventions, spanning traditional fantasy ancestries, fifth edition character classes, settlements, taverns, and factions. Because all procedural generation executes strictly client-side within your web browser using deterministic seeded algorithms, the site functions without user accounts, server tracking, or subscription paywalls. Players, authors, and game masters are granted unrestricted freedom to use, modify, and publish any generated name across personal home games, commercial actual-play livestreams, tabletop roleplaying supplements, and fantasy fiction novels without attribution or royalty fees. Our mission is to preserve storytelling momentum by providing evocative, pronounceable names within seconds of rolling initiative.',
      'The site uses static pages and browser-side generation. It does not require an account, and it does not send the names you create to a server.'
    ]
  },
  {
    heading: 'Original sounds, open-ended stories',
    paragraphs: [
      'Each ancestry uses syllable tables written for DnD Arena. The examples are original combinations rather than copied lists. A style is a sound prompt, not a rule about a character’s background or personality.',
      'The goal is a helpful starting point. Change a syllable, attach a family custom, or give a result a meaning your table invents.'
    ]
  },
  {
    heading: 'A growing set of focused tools',
    paragraphs: [
      'The first collection covers fantasy names by ancestry, family names, towns, taverns, parties, and quick non-player character prompts. Each tool has its own page so people can start with the task they came to do.',
      'More tools belong here only when they can offer a clear use and original material of their own.'
    ]
  }
];
---
<ContentPage
  title="About DnD Arena: Original Fantasy Name Tools"
  description="Learn who builds DnD Arena, why the original fantasy name tools exist, and how the project keeps campaign preparation quick, private, and easy to use."
  path="/about/"
  heading="About DnD Arena"
  eyebrow="A small independent project"
  intro="DnD Arena is a browser-based collection of original fantasy naming tools for tabletop stories, campaign notes, and creative writing."
  sections={sections}
/>
